              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Carter G. Phillips, in Buckman, the Court struck down a state tort based on fraud on the FDA, holding that such a claim would inevitably conflict with the FDA\u2019s responsibility to police fraud."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, the present case involves a Michigan statute that makes proof of fraud on the FDA a prerequisite for state tort liability, raising the same federal\u2011state conflict identified in Buckman."
      }
    ],
