            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether a statute that simply allowed a state tort action when FDA\u2011approved marketing conditions were not complied with would be permissible."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter questioned whether the admissibility of evidence depended on what the FDA would have done."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether there were reported cases showing the magnitude of the problem to the government."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked why the petitioner\u2019s argument that a jury should decide what the FDA would have done was incorrect, noting it could seriously interfere with the FDA\u2019s role."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg questioned whether taking depositions of FDA examiners would disrupt the agency\u2019s functions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether a state could prohibit evidence that a drug was FDA\u2011approved."
      }
    ],
