            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Carter G. Phillips, the case concerns whether state courts may hear tort claims that allege fraud on the FDA in the approval of a drug, an issue previously addressed in the Supreme Court\u2019s decision in Buckman."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5647d6f2d84d86b1d5aa2274e2e65b79ef173698de2eb4212ab68d47557f3e49",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5647d6f2d84d-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, the dispute raises questions about the balance between state tort law and the federal government\u2019s exclusive authority to police fraud on the FDA."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
